# Catppuccin themes for rio, tracked from our own fork
# (ningw42/rio @ feat/update-color-schema) rather than catppuccin/rio, pending
# the upstream PR. Files are taken verbatim -- there is no `filter` hook here
# any more; the fork fixes at the source what we used to patch on the way in.
#
# What upstream gets wrong, and the fork corrects:
#
# 1. ANSI black/white mapping. catppuccin's official style guide
#    (catppuccin/catppuccin, docs/style-guide.md, "ANSI Color Generation")
#    specifies for the dark flavors: Black 0 = Surface 1, Black 8 = Surface 2,
#    White 7 = Subtext 0, White 15 = Subtext 1 -- and for latte: Subtext 1 /
#    Subtext 0 / Surface 2 / Surface 1. catppuccin/rio has White 7 and White 15
#    swapped on frappe, macchiato and mocha, so the "bright" white slot is
#    darker than the normal one. That inversion is what made PSReadLine's
#    default inline-prediction color (`e[97;2;3m`, bright white + faint) render
#    *brighter* than surrounding text: rio resolves SGR 2 by palette
#    substitution, LightWhite -> White (rio-vt/src/config/colors/mod.rs,
#    to_dim()). The fork restores the guide's mapping, so the profile no longer
#    needs its `e[90;3m` workaround.
#
# 2. `tabs`. rio >= 0.4 replaced the old tab bar with the "island" strip and
#    repurposed `tabs` from the tab-bar BACKGROUND to the INACTIVE TAB TITLE
#    TEXT (renderer/mod.rs hands `tabs`/`tabs-active` to Island::new as the
#    inactive and active text colors; the island fills are derived from the
#    window background's luminance and are not themeable). Upstream still
#    carries <= 0.3 semantics and sets `tabs` to each flavor's `base`, painting
#    inactive tab titles in the background color, i.e. invisible. The fork sets
#    it to Subtext 0 and drops the three keys 0.4 deleted from the Colors struct
#    (`tabs-foreground`, `tabs-active-foreground`, `tabs-active-highlight`),
#    while adding the 0.4+ keys upstream never gained: `vi-cursor`, `split`,
#    `split-active`, `search-match-*` and `hint-*`.
#
# 3. `dim-*`. rio derives its whole dim ramp when a `dim-*` key is ABSENT
#    (rio-vt/src/config/colors/term.rs, `normal * DIM_FACTOR` at 0.66), but
#    upstream sets all nine to verbatim copies of their normal counterparts --
#    so `dim-foreground` equalled `foreground` and SGR 2 was a no-op. codex-cli
#    draws its entire session header that way (box border, version string,
#    `model:`, `directory:`, ` to change` are all faint over the default fg) and
#    came out pure white. The fork differentiates `dim-foreground`, `dim-black`
#    and `dim-white`. Note the style guide is silent on dim colors, so those
#    values are a judgement call, not a conformance requirement -- and deleting
#    the keys instead would be wrong for latte, where `* 0.66` darkens text
#    against a light background and makes "faint" more prominent than normal.
#
# Known remaining gap: the six chromatic `light-*` slots are still copies of
# their normal counterparts in both upstream and the fork. The guide generates
# them (dark: lightness * 0.94, chroma + 8, hue + 2; latte: lightness * 1.09,
# hue + 2) -- e.g. mocha `light-red` should be #f37799, not #f38ba8.
#
# The URLs track a BRANCH, so any push to feat/update-color-schema changes these
# bytes and fails the checksum on the next apply. That is the intended tripwire.
# Refresh with `python update_externals.py` after an intentional push; once the
# PR merges, repoint these back at catppuccin/rio main and refresh once more.
